{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792248599,"nonce":"BS2B1CQe8+scuCMTZRXHMGe99U0=","title":"A side module's WASI call fails in the native host: missing required memory export","message":"Reported by ashui-f2 (ashui git-bug 0c8c9a0). blinc_abi.wasm, a Rust side module, imports one WASI function (wasi_snapshot_preview1.random_get, for std's HashMap seeding). Under 'ash run' it loads, then traps on the first call with 'missing required memory export'. The host answers a library's WASI imports with its ordinary WASI functions, which read and write guest memory through the export named 'memory' of the instance that calls them; a side module imports the program's memory and exports none. sqlite.wasm never reached a WASI import, which is why it worked.\n\nFix: export the imported memory from the module as 'memory' before it is compiled (ash_wasm_link::dylink::expose_memory, called from the native loader). The browser host does not go through the calling instance, so it is unchanged.","files":null}]}